{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And bread, loaves.</b> [Mixed with] oil, and the proof is the verse: 'unleavened wafers'." "And he mentioned <b>in oil</b> — it is olive oil as customary. <b>And the word solet.</b> In Arabic it is samīd, from which the coarse bran has been removed from the wheat, and in the land of Ishmael they make it so, and there is no bread more esteemed than it. Many interpreted it from the root of 'I was misled from Your statutes' (Psalms 119:118), 'You have made an end of all the mighty ones of HaShem' (Lamentations 1:15), and similar to it is 'wheat from Kollah for your household' (1 Kings 5:25). And some say: ground fine.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:59.341322632Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}